  "verified": [
    "The service measures a settled or contacting released prop. A sampled miss, unretired dependent binding, self-retirement destination and absent samples each reject before a successful repaired transaction.",
    "The accepted grip keeps the item pose, moves its dependent binding and retires the exact physics body in one revision. The retired ID and its collision ray no longer hit. Native receipts replay exactly.",
    "CoreCLR and Windows Native AOT drop and then attempt pickup. A miss preserves the proxy. A live serialized reference blocks retirement. A later invalid callback rolls back an earlier successful pickup and its queued save.",
    "After a semantic pickup input, the item follows the moving joint. The managed callback reads the prior result, same-tick saves contain the committed state, and fresh processes reproduce the same archives.",
    "The 0.0.259 host rejects the new named feature. Its unchanged CoreCLR and Native AOT release consumers still run on 0.0.260."
  ],
